The exact computation of the Euler characteristic within thick graphs often proves to be computationally infeasible, thus researchers rely on probabilistic estimates. We present an efficient method to determine the genus of thick graphs within constant time. genus(G) ≤ 2/9 * chi(G) + 7/9 * sqrt(genus(T)) + 5/3, where:
- genus(G) denotes the genus of a thick graph G;
- chi(G) stands for the Euler characteristic within thick graphs;
- genus(T) represents the genus of the thin graph counterpart resulting from G's simplification;
- genus(T) can be computed in O(|G|) time, where |G| stands for the order of graph G;
- or, if we disregard the order of graph G, we can obtain an efficient estimation in O(log log |G|).
